assets.prompt:
Create a high-resolution, photorealistic MATERIAL AND CONSTRUCTION DETAIL SHEET for the exact same mass-timber fire station. Use a clean 3-by-2 grid of six equal close-up panels with thin neutral separators and no captions or typography. Every panel must be front-facing, evenly lit, perspective-correct and tileable enough to guide PBR texture creation:
1) honey-toned vertical timber rainscreen with fine grain, narrow shadow joints, subtle board-to-board variation and concealed fasteners;
2) exposed glulam column/beam corner showing laminated layers, end grain, joinery plate and a realistic warm matte clearcoat;
3) shou sugi ban charred-black vertical timber cladding with alligator grain, restrained charcoal variation and deep joints;
4) pale board-formed concrete with horizontal form-board grain, tie holes, crisp arrises and minor realistic staining;
5) green-roof meadow edge section showing dark metal flashing, gravel fire break, sedum, native grasses, yellow/purple wildflowers and roof build-up depth;
6) dark photovoltaic panel, standing-seam/parapet flashing and black metal apparatus-door frame detail with realistic roughness.
Match the materials, colour temperatures and construction quality of the supplied fire-station images exactly. Architectural product photography, sharp microdetail, neutral daylight, physically based surfaces. No cartoon, decorative collage styling, hands, tools, labels, logos, text, watermark or invented materials.
